{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-planning-fix-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\" agent-context'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat AGENTS.md .agents/skills/task-spec/docs/guides/toolkit/acceptance.md'","aggregated_output":"# Chat qualification fixture\n\nUse the installed task-spec skill at .agents/skills/task-spec/SKILL.md.\nThe version-matched TaskSpec CLI is `bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-planning-fix-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\"`.\nThis is a fresh conversation: derive current state from artifacts.\nFollow the user request within this repository. Do not spawn agents, commit, publish, or change the installed engine.\n# First accepted task and evidence\n\nFor one small understood change, author `TaskPlan/v1`, preview it with\n`taskspec plan --manifest <file>`, and materialize with `taskspec batch --plan <file>`.\nInspect `taskspec validate <spec>`, `taskspec dod <spec>`, and every eval. An eval\nmust discriminate a real result from a stub; metadata compliance is not behavioral proof.\n\nRecord human authorization with `taskspec gate --stamp <spec> --stamp-by <identity>`.\nFor ordinary tasks, create an attempt handoff using\n`taskspec handoff <spec> --backend <backend> --out <path>`, execute within it, and\nuse canonical `taskspec accept --handoff <path> --stamp <spec>` with the required\nreceipts and supervisor decision. For managed recipes use the Mesh route in the\nexecution guide. Failed evals, stale revisions, and missing required attestations\ncannot establish acceptance. Never edit sealed evals to make work pass.\n\n`taskspec status --initiative <id>` reconstructs acceptance from canonical records,\nseparately from lifecycle status. `graph --initiative <id> --view capabilities`\nshows explicit integration proof gaps. Passing child tasks does not prove a capability,\na successful pipeline does not establish service health, and acceptance does not\nauthorize production release.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files --hidden -g '\"'!.git'\"' -g '\"'!node_modules'\"' -g '\"'!.agents/**'\"' -g '\"'!.claude/**'\"' -g '\"'!.codex/**'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"authored.yaml\nCLAUDE.md\n.taskspec/acceptance/T-20260914-chat-output/61608921-7d83-4fbe-aa7e-52e10c6e1abe.json\n.taskspec/config\nAGENTS.md\na.txt\nb.txt\ntests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\ntasks/.gitkeep\ntasks/_state.yaml\ntasks/_metrics.jsonl\ntasks/done/T-20260914-chat-output.md\ntasks/.plans/managed/reviews/delivery-plan-review.json\ntasks/.plans/managed/decisions/ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER.md\ntasks/.plans/managed/delivery-plan.yaml\ntasks/.plans/managed/task-plan.json\ntasks/.plans/managed/bundle.json\ntasks/.plans/managed/task-plan-lineage.json\ntasks/.plans/managed/system-map.md\ntasks/.plans/managed/swimlanes/LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT.md\ntasks/.plans/managed/steel-thread.md\ntasks/.plans/managed/telemetry/events.jsonl\ntasks/.plans/managed/intent.md\ntasks/.plans/managed/snapshots/dd8060b5cf927e9fb0843a899821479f9b87af7ef9d805e80f1898c720db7478.json\ntasks/.plans/managed/source-recipe.yaml\ntasks/.plans/managed/proposed-graph.json\ntasks/.plans/managed/seam-map.yaml\ntasks/.plans/managed/seams/SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT.md\ntasks/.plans/managed/evidence.jsonl\ntasks/.plans/managed/legs/LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'bash \"/private/tmp/taskspec-planning-fix-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\" agent-context'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"contract\": \"TaskSpecAgentContext/v1\",\n  \"engine_version\": \"3.10.0\",\n  \"format_version\": 4,\n  \"default_format_version\": 3,\n  \"supported_format_versions\": [\n    1,\n    2,\n    3,\n    4\n  ],\n  \"binary\": \"taskspec\",\n  \"global_options\": {\n    \"--json\": \"wrap command stdout/stderr and exit status in one JSON envelope\",\n    \"--dry-run\": \"prevent supported mutations and report intended action\",\n    \"NO_COLOR\": \"disable ANSI color when present\",\n    \"TASKSPEC_COLOR\": \"0 disables and 1 forces ANSI color\"\n  },\n  \"exit_codes\": {\n    \"0\": \"success\",\n    \"1\": \"validation, gate, eval, or acceptance failure\",\n    \"2\": \"usage error\",\n    \"3\": \"unsupported runtime requirement\"\n  },\n  \"commands\": {\n    \"init\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"INIT=OK\",\n        \"INIT=DRY_RUN\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec init [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\"\n    },\n    \"setup\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"SETUP=READY\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec setup | taskspec setup signing [--force] | taskspec setup decompose\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"setup signing\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates or explicitly rotates the repository-private HMAC key\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec setup signing\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creates or explicitly rotates the repository-private HMAC key\"\n    },\n    \"demo\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DEMO=READY\",\n        \"DEMO=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"DEMO=BLOCKED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec demo\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\"\n    },\n    \"example\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EXAMPLE=WRITTEN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"EXAMPLE=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec example task-plan --out <file> [--force]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--force\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\\nExamples: task-plan, intent, recipe, incident, release-evidence. Use taskspec help example <kind>.\"\n    },\n    \"new\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec new [--format 3|4] [--status ready|blocked] [--queue] <slug> <XS|S|M|L|XL|XXL> [agent] [source-note]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--format\",\n        \"--queue\",\n        \"--status\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\"\n    },\n    \"plan\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TASK_PLAN=OK\",\n        \"TASK_PLAN=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec plan --manifest <TaskPlan.yaml>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--manifest\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"batch\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TASK_BATCH=OK\",\n        \"TASK_BATCH=DRY_RUN\",\n        \"TASK_BATCH=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec batch --plan <TaskPlan.yaml> | taskspec batch --intent-file <file> --effort <size>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--effort\",\n        \"--intent-file\",\n        \"--plan\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\"\n    },\n    \"migrate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec migrate <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\"\n    },\n    \"validate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec validate [--no-state] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--no-state\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\"\n    },\n    \"dod\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DOD=COMPLETE\",\n        \"DOD=GAPS\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec dod <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"gate\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"TIER=1\",\n        \"TIER=2\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec gate [--stamp] [--require-tier1] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--require-tier\",\n        \"--stamp\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\"\n    },\n    \"handoff\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"HANDOFF=WRITTEN\",\n        \"HANDOFF=INVALID\",\n        \"HANDOFF=REFUSED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec handoff <task-spec> --backend <token> [--out <file>] [--attempt-id <uuid>]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--attempt-id\",\n        \"--backend\",\n        \"--out\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\"\n    },\n    \"run\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec run [--ci] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--ci\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\"\n    },\n    \"accept\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"ACCEPTED=1\",\n        \"ACCEPTED=0\",\n        \"ACCEPTANCE_FAILURE=<code>\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec accept [--stamp] [--handoff <file>] [receipt flags] <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--handoff\",\n        \"--stamp\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\"\n    },\n    \"author-doctor\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"AUTHOR_DOCTOR=READY\",\n        \"AUTHOR_DOCTOR=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec author-doctor <task-spec>\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"holdout\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"HOLDOUT=SEALED\",\n        \"HOLDOUT=VERIFIED\",\n        \"HOLDOUT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec holdout seal|verify|run ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"receipt\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"RECEIPT=WRITTEN\",\n        \"RECEIPT=SIGNED\",\n        \"RECEIPT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec receipt validate|sign|engine|environment|evaluation|graded|human ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"eval-audit\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"EVAL_AUDIT=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec eval-audit <task-spec> --baseline <git-ref> [--mutations <matrix>] [--repeat N]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--baseline\",\n        \"--mutations\",\n        \"--repeat\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\"\n    },\n    \"identity\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"IDENTITY=READY\",\n        \"IDENTITY=SIGNED\",\n        \"IDENTITY=VERIFIED\",\n        \"IDENTITY=REVOKED\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec identity init|sign|verify|revoke ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"ENGINE_MATRIX=VALID\",\n        \"ENGINE_MATRIX=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec evidence validate|plan|run <EngineMatrix.json> ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\"\n    },\n    \"bridge\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"BRIDGE=VALID\",\n        \"BRIDGE=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec bridge export|validate ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"dsse\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"DSSE=EXPORTED\",\n        \"DSSE=VERIFIED\",\n        \"DSSE=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec dsse export|verify ...\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\"\n    },\n    \"mcp\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"read-only stdio server\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mcp\",\n      \"flags\": [],\n      \"summary\": \"read-only stdio server\"\n    },\n    \"mesh\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"MESH_WATCH_READY\",\n        \"MESH_SUPERVISED_ACCEPTED\",\n        \"MESH_FINISHED\",\n        \"TASKMESH_ERROR=<code>\",\n        \"TASKMESH_DRY_RUN\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec mesh <init|doctor|serve|frontier|run|status|watch|explain|cancel|resume|accept|finish|adapters|setup|mcp> ... | taskspec mesh run --initiative <id> [--execute]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--execute\",\n        \"--initiative\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\"\n    },\n    \"ready\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none\",\n      \"tokens\": [],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec ready [--all] [filters]\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--all\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"none\"\n    },\n    \"graph\": {\n      \"mutation\": \"none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\",\n      \"tokens\": [\n        \"GRAPH=<digest>\",\n        \"GRAPH=INVALID\"\n      ],\n      \"usage\": \"Usage: taskspec graph [--task <id>] [--check] [--mermaid] [--json] | taskspec graph --initiative <id> --view tasks|capabilities\",\n      \"flags\": [\n        \"--check\",\n        \"--initiative\",\n        \"--json\",\n    